  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin has $10.6B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The company won 141 awards so far, with an average award size of $74.9M, and obligations are up 1.4% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $7.1B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, then dipped to $7.3B in FY24 before climbing to $10.4B in FY25 and reaching $10.6B in FY26. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for the bulk of current-year obligations at $9.6B. Other notable NAICS markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $62.7M. The FY2026 portfolio is concentrated in missile and space vehicle work, while smaller streams of obligations appear in consulting, R&D, and various equipment manufacturing niches. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the page reports contract obligations except for award-value figures in certain tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Lockheed Martin's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $8.7B in FY23, then fell to $7.3B in FY24 before increasing to $10.4B in FY25 and $10.6B in FY26. Year-over-year obligations are up 1.4% for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. Award activity shows 141 awards so far with an average award size of $74.9M, indicating larger individual awards this year. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Lockheed Martin's FY2026 obligations concentrate by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market at $9.6B. Other notable markets are Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $62.7M. Remaining obligations are spread across consulting, R&D, engineering, and several manufacturing subcategories with values down to $69.8K."
      }
    ]
