      "q": "How much does Lockheed Martin make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Lockheed Martin has $10.6B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $8.7B in FY23, dipped to $7.3B in FY24, and then increased to $10.4B in FY25 before reaching $10.6B in FY26. The company has won 141 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $74.9M, and obligations are up 1.4% year over year."
